  "title": "Retire six writing rules into unplaceable-reference",
  "summary": "Six writing rules (bare-reference, reference-without-label, reference-without-link, chat-local-reference, undefined-name, undefined-name-at-start) are collapsed into the single unplaceable-reference rule, which now also carries the link warning for labelled-but-unlinked repo references. Because ids disappear, every place a user could still name one — suppression markers, writing.levels overrides, osf-expect declarations, osf explain, and the OSF_WRITING_CHAT_LOCAL_LABELS env var — is taught to say the id is gone and name its replacement instead of failing silently or with a bare 'not a rule id'.",
